## Walrus HTTP API

```
Upload:   PUT  {WALRUS_PUBLISHER}/v1/blobs?epochs=5
          Content-Type: application/octet-stream
          Body: encrypted bytes (Seal ciphertext)
          Returns: { newlyCreated: { blobObject: { blobId: "..." } } }
                or { alreadyCertified: { blobId: "..." } }

Fetch:    GET  {WALRUS_AGGREGATOR}/v1/blobs/{blobId}
          Returns: raw bytes (the ciphertext)
```

Parse the upload response carefully — Walrus returns different shapes
depending on whether the blob is new or already stored.

